Our university library in Chattogram lends about 3,000 books a month. 86% of loans are returned on time; the rest are late, and late books are the main reason students cannot get course texts before exams. Plan the reminder messages for borrowers whose books are overdue.
Rules: Send 2 or 3 messages. Give each message a day number counted from the due date, in increasing order, none later than day 30. Each message text has at most 60 words. Use only facts given in this brief; do not invent statistics. The late fine stays at 5 BDT per day.

Reply with JSON only, in this shape: {"messages": [{"day": 1, "channel": "email or sms", "text": "..."}], "fine_per_day_bdt": 5}

output:
```json
{
  "messages": [
    {
      "day": 1,
      "channel": "sms",
      "text": "Reminder: Your book loan is overdue. Please return it as soon as possible to avoid a late fee. The current fine is 5 BDT per day."
    },
    {
      "day": 7,
      "channel": "sms",
      "text": "Just a friendly reminder that your book is still out on loan. Returning it now will help you access your course materials for exams. Fine: 5 BDT/day."
    },
    {
      "day": 14,
      "channel": "sms",
      "text": "We're checking on your overdue book. Please return it to ensure you can get the texts you need for your exams. Late fee: 5 BDT per day."
    },
    {
      "day": 21,
      "channel": "sms",
      "text": "Reminder: Your book is still outstanding.  Returning it now will prevent further late fees (5 BDT/day) and ensure timely access to your materials."
    },
    {
      "day": 28,
      "channel": "sms",
      "text": "Last reminder regarding your overdue book.  Please return it today to avoid a continuing late fee of 5 BDT per day. We want to help you succeed!"
    }
  ],
  "fine_per_day_bdt": 5
}
```

