messages.content:
Write an incident policy for the course-registration website our student club maintains (6 volunteer developers, 2 of them maintainers).
Rules: at most 4 rules; every rule must say who may trigger it; include one rule for database outages.

Reply with JSON only, in this shape: {"rules": [{"trigger": "...", "action": "...", "who_can_trigger": "..."}]}

output:
```json
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "trigger": "Student requests a course registration change (add/remove)",
      "action": "Developer must review the request, verify eligibility (prerequisites, enrollment limits), and confirm the change with the student before processing.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any volunteer developer"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "Database outage or significant performance degradation affecting course registration functionality",
      "action": "Maintainer must immediately notify all developers and the club president.  A backup database should be tested and prepared for potential switchover.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Maintainer"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "A student reports a bug or error in the course registration system (e.g., incorrect display of available courses, payment issues)",
      "action": "Developer assigned to the bug report must investigate, fix the issue, and thoroughly test the solution before deploying the fix.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Any volunteer developer"
    },
    {
      "trigger": "A new course is added to the system by an administrator (outside the club)",
      "action": "Maintainer must verify the course details (name, credits, prerequisites) against official university records and update the database accordingly.  Document the source of the information.",
      "who_can_trigger": "Maintainer"
    }
  ]
}
```

